 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Add `FilesService.Upload(ctx, fileName, content, ...)`, matching the
+  convention already used by `CallLogsService.AddRecording` and product image
+  uploads: callers pass a file name and an `io.Reader` instead of building the
+  multipart body themselves. The body is encoded internally via
+  `multipartbody.NewFile`, which always produces a `*bytes.Reader`. Because
+  `http.NewRequestWithContext` only auto-populates `Request.GetBody` for
+  `*bytes.Buffer`, `*bytes.Reader`, and `*strings.Reader`, the resulting
+  request is always replayable, so uploads through `Upload` retry correctly on
+  429/5xx even when `content` wraps a non-seekable source such as an
+  `*os.File`. `FilesService.Add` is unchanged and still expects a pre-built
+  multipart body; a body it doesn't recognize as one of those three types
+  (for example one wrapping an `*os.File` directly) still won't be retried,
+  since the retry transport can't replay it.
+
